urs or more than 9 hours. It does not directly challenge the conclusion that maintaining an appropriate amount of sleep (about 7 hours) is necessary to improve cognitive ability. It explains the observed behavior but does not refute the researchers' conclusion.\n\nAfter evaluating all options, the one that best questions the researchers' views is:\n</think>\n<answer>\nB) People who sleep for about 7 hours a day are all over 70 years old.\n</answer>",
