e to dislike the client.\n\nC) **Some employees of telemarketing agencies are unlikely to be certain about whether trying to talk someone into buying the product of a client of the agency after the person has said that he or she does not want to will likely engender animosity toward the client.**\n   - This option introduces uncertainty about the likelihood of engendering animosity. While it might be true, it does not directly justify the application. The application is based on the certainty that such actions will engender animosity.\n\nD) **People who are already predisposed to dislike the client of a telemarketing agency are more likely to refuse to buy the product of that client than are people who are predisposed to like the client.**\n   - This option discusses the predisposition of people to dislike the client. However, it does not directly address the situation where the person explicitly states they do not want to buy the product. This option does not justify the application.\n\nAfter evaluating all the options, the one that directly justifies the given application of the principle is Option B.\n</think>\n<answer>\nB\n</answer>",
